CHANGED: The normalization strategies are described as pure values of a strategy DSL (`Clash.Normalize.Strategy.Spec`, `Clash.Rewrite.StrategyDSL`) in which transformations declare the `Term` constructors they can fire on, and are compiled once at strategy-construction time (`Clash.Rewrite.StrategyDSL.Compile`) into fused dispatch code: one constructor match per node drives both the selection of applicable transformations and the descent into the node's children. Measured ~24% faster HDL generation end-to-end on a large industrial design, without changing the produced HDL. Only debug output changes: `-fclash-debug-transformations` no longer prints "Trying:" lines for transformations that structurally cannot match a node.
